\begin_layout Paragraph
Closing the gap
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The explainability gap represents the learning effort one has to make from
 one's previous knowledge to solve a black box.
 For optimal interpretability of policies, they should be as close as possible
 to the expert policy while having the performance of the blackbox.
 To close this gap between the expert's approach and a black box, which
 is better, it would therefore be optimal to show the expert what he would
 have to change in his code to become more like the black box.
\end_layout

